    "steps": [
      "Put the bones in a large pot, cover with water, boil for 5 minutes, then drain and rinse the bones and pot to remove scum.",
      "Return the bones to the pot with 4 litres of cold water and the brisket. Bring to a gentle simmer and skim.",
      "Toast the star anise, cinnamon, cloves and coriander seeds in a dry pan for 1 minute until fragrant. Add them to the pot with the charred onion and ginger.",
      "Simmer very gently, partly covered, for 3 hours, removing the brisket after about 1 hour 30 minutes when tender; put it in cold water for 10 minutes so it stays moist, then slice.",
      "Strain the broth, then season with the fish sauce, sugar and salt. It should taste slightly oversalted, since it will be diluted by the noodles.",
      "Cook the noodles as directed, drain, and divide among bowls. Add the brisket and the raw sliced beef.",
      "Bring the broth to a rolling boil and ladle it over the beef, which will cook in the heat. Serve with the herbs, sprouts, lime and chilli."
    ],
    "notes": "The broth improves if it is cooled overnight and the fat is lifted off before reheating.",
